</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p><strong>Item:</strong> SCP-████</p>
<p><strong>Tissue Test Record:</strong><br />
[Data Expunged]</p>
<p><strong>Termination Test Record:</strong><br />
[Data Expunged]</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> Dr. [Redacted]</p>
<p><strong>Item:</strong> SCP-682</p>
<p><strong>Tissue Test Record:</strong><br />
Denied by O5 Command.</p>
<p><strong>Termination Test Record:</strong><br />
SCP-682 was brought into SCP-5942's old containment area/Testing chamber, screams of the two entities continue for 4 days, at which point the noise abruptly stops. Video feeds reveal SCP-682 with 99% of its initial mass absent and huddled in the southwest corner. Feed shows SCP-5942 on the east end of the room with about 30% its initial mass absent. SCP-5942 was regenerating from injuries and SCP-682 is displaying signs of being infected with AML F7437, and laughing as if it was in euphoria.</p>
<p>When SCP-5942 was asked &quot;how was your encounter&quot; with SCP-682 SCP-5942 will react with rage.<br />
SCP-5942 was asked why it reacted with rage when 682 was mentioned and resulted in a containment breach (seven-thousandth occurrence) with in heavy casualties.</p>
<p>Note: Dr. [Redacted] was terminated for disobeying orders from O5 Command and 682 and 5942 was not to be Cross-tested, the one who gave the order to Cross-test will be terminated or punished severely.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Item:</strong> SCP-173 with a photograph of SCP-096's face attached to it</p>
<p><strong>Tissue Test Record:</strong><br />
N/A</p>
<p><strong>Termination Test Record:</strong><br />
Denied by O5-██</p>
<p>Notes: No. Hell NO. Setting aside the problem of the SCP-682 and SCP-5942 Cross test, a SCP-173 that cannot be observed for fear of triggering a response from SCP-096 is a self-perpetuating catastrophe that the Foundation does not, under any reasonable circumstances, have the slightest desire to unleash and 5942 will probably let all the other anomalies at Site 19 out. Denied with vehemence.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> Dr. [Redacted]</p>
<p><strong>Item:</strong> An Ordinary Gaming PC</p>
<p><strong>Tissue Test Record:</strong><br />
N/A</p>
<p><strong>Termination Test Record:</strong><br />
[Data Lost]</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Item:</strong> SCP-662</p>
<p><strong>Tissue Test Record:</strong><br />
N/A</p>
<p><strong>Termination Test Record:</strong><br />
Mr. Deeds is summoned, and asked if he can destroy SCP-5942 permanently.</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds' response: &quot;I'm terribly sorry, sir, I'm afraid I can't.&quot;</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds is asked if he can kill SCP-5942.</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds' response: &quot;Again, sir, I'm terribly sorry, but I'm afraid I can't.&quot;</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds is asked if he can incapacitate SCP-5942.</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds' response: &quot;As a matter of fact… depending on how sir means the word 'incapacitate', and depending on how long sir wishes the creature to be incapacitated… yes for a few seconds at most.&quot;</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds is asked to expand on how he would perform such an action.</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds' response: &quot;Sir, the simplest and quickest method — which I must point out would not be the most efficient — would be for me to offer myself up for the creature to devour me; certainly its offensive capacities would be lessened whilst it is occupied in consuming my flesh. This would be simplest as it requires no preparation on my part, sir, but I'm certain you'll understand that the overall effect on the creature would be insignificant. Were I to engage the creature in combat, either with or without weapons, I could certainly occupy its attention and offensive capacities for a longer interval; unfortunately, I'm afraid the creature would eventually defeat me, at which point it would begin consuming my flesh as I have previously described. However, I could certainly booby-trap my person with a variety of noxious substances - soporifics, perhaps, or explosives, or perhaps encapsulated neurotoxins, or even [REDACTED], so that when the creature does inevitably consume me, it sustains further damage. That said, sir, I must remind you that the creature's tendency towards regeneration means that any damage I inflict would be sadly temporary about a few seconds at most.&quot;</p>
<p>Mr. Deeds is thanked and dismissed.</p>
<p>Note: Mr. Deeds' knowledge of [REDACTED] is not to be considered a security breach.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Item:</strong> ●●|●●●●●|●●|●</p>
